# rx_pop_closed.tkr — the §10 C1 Gap-2 de-risk fixture. It proves the composition no shipped generic
# previously exercised: a generic method whose return is a union of the type-param and a NOMINAL
# (non-`null`) member — `Rx<T>.pop(): T | Closed` — STAMPS at `Rx__g__i32` and matches on BOTH arms
# (`i32 as x` and `Closed`). The `V | null` generic-union-return precedent (Dictionary.get) proves the
# type-param-member half; the nominal-variant two-level match proves the `Closed` half; this fixture
# pins their composition. A self-contained project (its own local `Rx<T>`/`Closed`, since the
# teko::threads surface is a compiler-internal leaf). Runs on the C backend.

Feature: rx_pop_closed — a generic Rx<T>.pop(): T | Closed stamps and matches on both arms

  Scenario: pop_values_then_closed — pop two i32 then the Closed sentinel, summing to 3
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
